A||||34||Archie||Why, all of a sudden, is copying OK?||||1||
Z||000000||Archie||10-14-2001||10:08 PM||||Pat Jon Kalsmith, I consider you a friend of mine, you are a past customer of mine and a long time Fiero enthusiast. You are a founding member of NIFE and that carries a lot of weight with me. I regret that I have to write this and hope that you take it in the sprit in which it is written.<P>As most people who read this forum know, IRM is indeed still in business. Jim Sutter is not on this Forum but still owns and runs IRM. Of all the Vendors that anyone here can name (including myself) Jim has been serving the needs of Fiero owners longer than anybody.<P>Many will recall a resent thread where TFS was openly copying some of Rodney's products. Everyone here had a "Fit" to protect Rodney & I agree with everyone's opinion that TFS was Way in the wrong here. Everyone got involved because the guy who was being copied is an active member of this Forum. Where is all that outrageous indignation now?<P>In the case of Fibersmith we have just the opposite..... the person doing the copying is a Forum member & the person who is being copied is not Internet active. Whether a person is represented on this forum or not should not be the governing factor as to whether copying should be acceptable to us.<P>Now Jon, I'm aware that you've copied other peoples' products and maybe I should have spoken up earlier. However, this time, you are copying someone who has been faithfully serving the Fiero community longer than ANYONE else on this forum. <P>On you Web Site you state "Fibersmith gives you the look you want at a price you can afford." Which leads me to believe that the only reason you are copying the work of others is not to improve the product but only to address price. You have made it clear that you are copying EXACTLY the Integrated Rocker Panels from IRM. This is not fair.... anyone who copies the products of others should be able to sell cheaper because he has no investment in R&D and no vested interest in the product.<P>Now Jon, I feel your business can be a very valuable asset to the Fiero community, but I  ask you to do onto others as you would have them do unto you. Please originate some items of your own design and the world will be knocking on your door. When You've done some of your own products, then you'll want us to help you protect them. This is not a 2 way street... Fair is Fair.<P>You will find more on this topic at <A HREF="http://home.v8archie.com/arch5.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.v8archie.com/arch5.htm</A> <P>Regards<P>Archie<P>Do onto others as you would have them do unto you.||||reg||1
